{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"CVE-2024-46754","state":"PUBLISHED","summary":"In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Remove tst_run from lwt_seg6local_prog_ops.\n\nThe syzbot reported that the lwt_seg6 related BPF ops can be invoked\nvia bpf_test_run() without wi…","description":"In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Remove tst_run from lwt_seg6local_prog_ops.\n\nThe syzbot reported that the lwt_seg6 related BPF ops can be invoked\nvia bpf_test_run() without without entering input_action_end_bpf()\nfirst.\n\nMartin KaFai Lau said that self test for BPF_PROG_TYPE_LWT_SEG6LOCAL\nprobably didn't work since it was introduced in commit 04d4b274e2a\n(\"ipv6: sr: Add seg6local action End.BPF\"). The reason is that the\nper-CPU variable seg6_bpf_srh_states::srh is never assigned in the self\ntest case but each BPF function expects it.\n\nRemove test_run for BPF_PROG_TYPE_LWT_SEG6LOCAL.","published":"2024-09-18T07:12:13.780Z","lastModified":"2026-09-02T12:49:13.346Z","withdrawn":null,"severity":{"overall":"HIGH","cvss":7.8},"cvss":{"v2":null,"v3_0":null,"v3_1":{"vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","baseScore":7.8,"baseSeverity":"HIGH","exploitabilityScore":null,"impactScore":null,"source":"cve.org"},"v4_0":null},"cwe":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"Linux","product":"Linux","cpe":null,"versions":[{"version":"004d4b274e2a1a895a0e5dc66158b90a7d463d44","status":"affected","versionEndExcluding":"ea3fae6984ba0f054550e4da22219489c12cd8d4","versionEndIncluding":null},{"version":"004d4b274e2a1a895a0e5dc66158b90a7d463d44","status":"affected","versionEndExcluding":"a675524cfbe88fd49c05ff8807a08646983e687c","versionEndIncluding":null},{"version":"004d4b274e2a1a895a0e5dc66158b90a7d463d44","status":"affected","versionEndExcluding":"b05c2e25a5c168dbb46b6f7fcb741fd4e4f3b54a","versionEndIncluding":null},{"version":"004d4b274e2a1a895a0e5dc66158b90a7d463d44","status":"affected","versionEndExcluding":"e217492f6fa2228ad703ee3006d8fc4e5969fbd4","versionEndIncluding":null},{"version":"004d4b274e2a1a895a0e5dc66158b90a7d463d44","status":"affected","versionEndExcluding":"9cd15511de7c619bbd0f54bb3f28e6e720ded5d6","versionEndIncluding":null},{"version":"004d4b274e2a1a895a0e5dc66158b90a7d463d44","status":"affected","versionEndExcluding":"c13fda93aca118b8e5cd202e339046728ee7dddb","versionEndIncluding":null}],"platforms":[]},{"vendor":"Linux","product":"Linux","cpe":null,"versions":[{"version":"4.18","status":"affected","versionEndExcluding":null,"versionEndIncluding":null},{"version":null,"status":"unaffected","versionEndExcluding":"4.18","versionEndIncluding":null},{"version":"5.10.269","status":"unaffected","versionEndExcluding":null,"versionEndIncluding":"5.10.*"},{"version":"5.15.220","status":"unaffected","versionEndExcluding":null,"versionEndIncluding":"5.15.*"},{"version":"6.1.187","status":"unaffected","versionEndExcluding":null,"versionEndIncluding":"6.1.*"},{"version":"6.6.156","status":"unaffected","versionEndExcluding":null,"versionEndIncluding":"6.6.*"},{"version":"6.10.10","status":"unaffected","versionEndExcluding":null,"versionEndIncluding":"6.10.*"},{"version":"6.11","status":"unaffected","versionEndExcluding":null,"versionEndIncluding":"*"}],"platforms":[]}],"configurations":[],"references":[{"url":"https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ea3fae6984ba0f054550e4da22219489c12cd8d4","source":"cve.org","tags":[]},{"url":"https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a675524cfbe88fd49c05ff8807a08646983e687c","source":"cve.org","tags":[]},{"url":"https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b05c2e25a5c168dbb46b6f7fcb741fd4e4f3b54a","source":"cve.org","tags":[]},{"url":"https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e217492f6fa2228ad703ee3006d8fc4e5969fbd4","source":"cve.org","tags":[]},{"url":"https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9cd15511de7c619bbd0f54bb3f28e6e720ded5d6","source":"cve.org","tags":[]},{"url":"https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c13fda93aca118b8e5cd202e339046728ee7dddb","source":"cve.org","tags":[]}],"exploit